## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with Android architecture components (Room, Flow/LiveData, ViewModel, RecyclerView) and basic lifecycle handling. It also checks state management across rotations with minimal boilerplate.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, and Database wiring
- Flow or LiveData for data observation
- ViewModel for lifecycle-aware state
- RecyclerView with DiffUtil for efficient updates
- Threading: Dispatchers.IO for DB ops

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity
data class Note(
  @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
  val content: String,
  val timestamp: Long
)
@Dao
interface NoteDao {
  @Insert
  suspend fun insert(note: Note)
  @Query("SELECT * FROM Note ORDER BY timestamp DESC")
  fun getAll(): Flow<List<Note>>
  @Delete
  suspend fun delete(note: Note)
}
@Database(entities = [Note::class], version = 1)
abstract class NoteDatabase : RoomDatabase() {
  abstract fun noteDao(): NoteDao
}
```

